# PengyOS — the shared stack that shadow's PAM files include (login, passwd,
# chsh, chfn, chpasswd, newusers, groupmems: "include system-auth").
# Without this file every one of them failed: console logins on a TTY or the
# serial port answered "Permission denied" (Server 26.10.3, when shadow was
# rebuilt with PAM; Core on 26.11.0, when shadow's login replaced BusyBox's, so
# the file moved to Core). Plain Unix accounts, as in `other`; sessions get
# limits, the environment and a logind session, as SSH logins do (pam.d/sshd).
auth      required  pam_env.so
auth      required  pam_unix.so
account   required  pam_unix.so
password  required  pam_unix.so sha512 shadow
session   required  pam_limits.so
session   required  pam_unix.so
session   optional  pam_systemd.so
